// Growth Asset Pack generation engine.
//
// Produces the four client-facing deliverables that make up the premium Client
// Acquisition Infrastructure Pack. Each part is generated by its own focused
// model call (so the output stays deep instead of shallow, and so a single
// deliverable can be regenerated on its own). All calls share the same grounding
// context: the real business profile plus the heuristic audit intelligence
// briefing.
//
// ── THE BUILD IS DATA, NOT PROSE (Phase 2) ───────────────────────────────────
// What ReclaimedHQ sells is fourteen named GoHighLevel workflows and one
// six-stage pipeline, and all of it is written down ONCE in
// src/lib/workflow-catalogue.ts. Every prompt below that describes the build
// renders it FROM that file rather than retyping it, and every workflow name,
// trigger and pipeline stage that reaches a document is STAMPED from it after
// generation. That is the whole anti-drift property: the proposal, the Blueprint,
// the asset pack and the timeline cannot describe four different builds, and a
// workflow added to the catalogue cannot go undescribed or uncopied.
//
// ── WHAT WAS REMOVED, AND WHERE ITS COPY WENT ────────────────────────────────
// This engine used to fire a tenth call that wrote a whole landing-page
// specification — page sections, hero options, a page order, a "tech stack"
// (the hint was literally "e.g. Framer") and deployment notes. We do not build,
// host, redesign or deploy websites. The one page we build is the booking page
// inside the client's GoHighLevel sub-account, so that call was writing for a
// surface the offer does not contain, and its deployment notes were instructions
// for work nobody was going to do.
//
// The call is gone. Its copy is NOT: generateConversionSurfaces() below writes
// the same material addressed to the surfaces that exist (booking page,
// lead-capture form, LeadGate front-end, webchat) plus an explicitly ADVISORY
// block for the client's own website. docs/landing-call-inventory.md is the
// asset-by-asset record of what was repointed and what was deliberately dropped.

